<title>BELGIUM: Belgian arms maker FN workers on 24-hour strike.</title>
<headline>Belgian arms maker FN workers on 24-hour strike.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The staff of Belgian arms maker FN Herstal began a 24-hour strike on Monday morning in protest at the lack of information from management on the company's financial position, Belgian television reported.</p>
<p>The decision followed the cancellation of a meeting that was due to have taken place in Versailles between the FN staff unions and the management of majority shareholder  Giat Industries.</p>
<p>A handful of staff picketted FN's gates, preventing the management entering the plant.</p>
